{
  "_note": "v3.5: same taxonomy + symptoms text as v3.4 but with the visual symptoms FIRST: tests whether v3.4's taxonomy dominated because of its position. Zero-shot ablation of ONE change against v3.4 (v3.4: HM 8.4% top-1 / 33.0% top-5; v3: 10.2% / 30.0%) (everything else identical; v3: HM 10.2% top-1 / 30.0% top-5). Zero-shot has no validation split (nothing is trained or tuned), so v3 vs this run on the same test images is the comparison; differences of a point or less are within what template wording alone can shift.",
  "_result": "Order is not the cause: putting the visual symptoms first gives the same result as v3.4 (HM 8.5% vs 8.4% top-1, 33.0% top-5 both; seen 9.4%, unseen 7.7%; grape_black_rot 21% vs 25%). Whatever the order, mixing taxonomy and symptoms in ONE sentence lets the taxonomy dominate the embedding.",
